    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d836">

                <pb facs="0843" n="731" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg731"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5465: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-24T16:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                                1919—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:53 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>4159. Helsingfors advises that no request for help has been made to Finland by
                    Judenitch as he as well as Denikin is opposed to possible <pb facs="0844"
                        n="732" xml:id="pg732"/> capture of Petrograd by Finnish troops. After fall
                    of Petrograd question of Finland’s possible intervention may be discussed.
                    [Repeated to] American Mission. Copy to London.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
